      "common:synonyms": [
        {
          "#text": "含贵金属废碎料；含贵金属可回收废料",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        },
        {
          "#text": "waste and scrap containing precious metals; recyclable waste containing precious metals",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        }
      ],
      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Scrap metal, used metals that are an important source of industrial metals and alloys, particularly in the production of steel, copper, lead, aluminum, and zinc. Smaller amounts of tin, nickel, magnesium, and precious metals are also recovered from scrap. Scrap consists of recyclable materials, usually metals, left over from product manufacturing and consumption, such as parts of vehicles, building supplies, and surplus materials. Unlike waste, scrap has monetary value, especially recovered metals, and non-metallic materials are also recovered for recycling.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "废金属，这是工业金属和合金的重要来源，特别是在生产钢铁、铜、铅、铝和锌的过程中。从废料中也可以回收少量的锡、镍、镁和贵金属。废料由可回收材料组成，通常是金属，这些金属是产品制造和消费的剩余物，如车辆部件、建筑供应品和剩余材料。与废物不同，废料具有货币价值，尤其是回收金属，非金属材料也被回收用于再循环。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
